---
import Policy from '../layouts/Policy.astro';
import OperatorContact from '../components/OperatorContact.astro';
const sections: [string, string][] = [
  ['operator', 'The service and operator'],
  ['account', 'Eligibility and accounts'],
  ['content', 'Your content and sharing'],
  ['ai', 'AI and external services'],
  ['billing', 'Subscriptions and credits'],
  ['use', 'Acceptable use'],
  ['availability', 'Changes and termination'],
  ['responsibility', 'Responsibility and rights'],
  ['law', 'Law, disputes and updates'],
];
---

<Policy
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms for using PaperEnjoyer’s website, accounts and online services."
  path="/terms"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="operator">
    <h2>1. The service and operator</h2>
    <p>
      PaperEnjoyer helps you organize papers, read PDFs, generate AI-assisted explanations, ask
      questions and synchronize a research library. These terms govern our website and online
      services. “We”, “us” and “our” refer to the service operator using the name PaperEnjoyer.
    </p>
    <OperatorContact />
    <p>
      The university is a correspondence location, not the provider or sponsor of PaperEnjoyer. By
      creating an account or using our online services, you agree to these terms. If you do not
      agree, do not use those services. The <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains data
      handling; the <a href="/refund">Refund Policy</a> addresses purchases.
    </p>
    <p>
      Any separately supplied software or open-source component remains subject to its applicable
      licence. These terms do not remove permissions granted by those licences.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="account">
    <h2>2. Eligibility and accounts</h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 18 and legally able to enter into this agreement. If you act for an
      organization, you must have authority to bind it. Provide accurate account information,
      protect your sign-in credentials and notify us if you suspect unauthorized access.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are responsible for activity you authorize through your account. Do not sell accounts,
      share credentials to evade limits or create accounts to abuse introductory offers. Keep copies
      of important research outside the service.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="content">
    <h2>3. Your content and sharing</h2>
    <p>
      You retain the rights you hold in uploaded papers, notes and other content. Only upload or
      share material you are entitled to process in the ways the feature requires. Access to a paper
      does not necessarily include permission to redistribute it or send it to an AI service.
    </p>
    <p>
      You give us a non-exclusive permission to store, copy, process and transmit your content to
      the extent needed to provide your requested features, secure the service and handle support.
      This includes processing by relevant service providers as described in the Privacy Policy. It
      is not a transfer of ownership.
    </p>
    <p>
      Unedited, generated standard reading results may be submitted automatically for administrator
      quality review and, if approved, reused for the same paper by other accounts. This feature is
      distinct from your private annotations, edited notes and independent Agent conversations. See{' '}
      <a href="/privacy#sharing">Standard readings and sharing</a> before processing confidential or
      restricted material.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you create a share link, you authorize access to the selected snapshot. Anyone who
      obtains the link may be able to view it, and recipients may save or import copies. Revoking
      the link cannot recall copies already obtained. You are responsible for the content and rights
      included in the snapshot.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not promise that AI output is unique, protectable by copyright or free of third-party
      rights. If you report an infringement, include the affected material, its location and a way
      to contact you; we may restrict access while reviewing the report.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="ai">
    <h2>4. AI and external services</h2>
    <p>
      AI output can be incomplete, inaccurate or fabricated, including citations, translations and
      equations. Verify results against the original paper. PaperEnjoyer provides research
      assistance, not professional medical, legal or financial advice.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cloud parsing and AI tasks send relevant materials to the services involved, including when
      library synchronization is disabled. Server-based reading can continue after the app closes.
      Local Agent execution can still communicate with the model provider you selected.
    </p>
    <p>
      Services you connect with your own account or API key have their own terms, prices and data
      practices. You are responsible for permission to use those services and their charges.
      Features and model availability depend on the selected provider and your access.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="billing">
    <h2>5. Subscriptions and credits</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/pricing">Pricing page</a> currently describes upcoming plans. Coming-soon plans,
      promotional credits and credit packs are not active entitlements of the current free app, and
      no purchase can be completed on this website yet.
    </p>
    <p>
      When paid checkout becomes available through Paddle, Paddle will be the reseller and merchant
      of record for those transactions. Its{' '}
      <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/buyer-terms">Buyer Terms</a> will govern the purchase
      from Paddle; these terms will govern your use of PaperEnjoyer. The checkout will identify the
      price, taxes, billing interval and applicable offer before you pay.
    </p>
    <p>
      Monthly plans will renew until cancelled. Cancel through the Paddle receipt’s
      subscription-management link or <a href="https://paddle.net/">Paddle support</a> before the
      next renewal. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the paid period. Refund requests are
      separate and follow our Refund Policy and applicable rights.
    </p>
    <p>
      Monthly allocations, rollover limits, expiry and promotion eligibility are described on the
      Pricing page. Monthly credits are spent before purchased credits. Purchased packs do not
      expire through a monthly reset or cancellation. The 300-Credit registration gift is
      promotional and expires after 30 days. Credits are service-use units, not cash, and cannot be
      transferred or redeemed for money except where a purchase refund or applicable law requires a
      remedy.
    </p>
    <p>
      After a downgrade, data above the new storage limit is retained, but new uploads are
      restricted until usage is within the limit or you upgrade. We will disclose material price or
      entitlement changes before they apply, including any notice or consent required by law. They
      will not retrospectively remove rights already acquired.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="use">
    <h2>6. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Do not use the service to infringe rights, distribute unlawful material, access another
      person’s data without permission, spread malware, disrupt the service or bypass security,
      usage limits or payment controls. Do not upload sensitive or confidential material unless you
      have authority for the processing and disclosures involved.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may apply proportionate limits to protect availability and investigate suspected abuse.
      Restrictions will not be used to remove rights granted under an applicable software licence.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="availability">
    <h2>7. Changes, suspension and termination</h2>
    <p>
      Maintenance, provider failures and security incidents can interrupt service. We cannot promise
      uninterrupted operation or any particular research outcome. We may change features or
      discontinue a service, with reasonable advance notice where practicable and with the remedies
      required for affected paid services.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may restrict or suspend an account for material breach, fraud, a security threat or a legal
      requirement. Where appropriate, we will explain the reason and allow a reasonable opportunity
      to resolve it; urgent risks or legal restrictions may require immediate action.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may stop using the service and request account deletion by email. Uninstalling the app
      alone does not delete cloud data or cancel a subscription. We will explain deletion
      consequences, outstanding billing and any necessary retention when handling your request. See
      the Privacy Policy for retention and recipient copies.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="responsibility">
    <h2>8. Responsibility and protected rights</h2>
    <p>
      We are responsible for providing the service with the care required by applicable law. You are
      responsible for your lawful use of content and for checking AI-assisted work before relying on
      it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing here excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, including for fraud,
      deliberate misconduct or other protected claims. Nothing removes mandatory consumer
      guarantees, data protection rights or remedies for a service that is defective or materially
      different from its description. No blanket waiver of those rights is required to use
      PaperEnjoyer.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="law">
    <h2>9. Law, disputes and updates</h2>
    <p>
      The laws of the People’s Republic of China govern our service agreement, subject to the
      mandatory protections available in your place of residence. You retain any right to bring a
      claim in a court available to you under applicable law. These terms do not impose mandatory
      arbitration or an exclusive foreign court on consumers. Paddle’s transaction terms address
      disputes with Paddle separately.
    </p>
    <p>
      Contact us first if you would like help resolving a concern; doing so is not a condition of
      exercising legal rights. We may update these terms as the service changes. We will date the
      updated version and provide additional notice or obtain agreement where required. Changes
      apply prospectively and do not remove existing purchase or statutory rights.
    </p>
  </section>
</Policy>
